#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4720" :question/problem "Let ![](images/38/38c4cba166fdfcd0954a18156946e41834a626cccee4baab976861dd23574c85.png) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/a4/a4a2b1035b3b5699ff3558ffa839fbd667ad6defaf30a158d628c7011ab97aa8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" :question/math-academy-id "e-4722" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d3/d35cb368b7380f08e486757813138fa3f3332ed40a9b0e5faeab7a20c3119bef.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/c8/c87dbe6c81a670dd62d8a130d3085b2e9b36d5d3ad27d53bda571ec69b639689.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090417bb-bda0-5586-94b2-46eceb1bcbb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263085} {:answer/id #uuid "1a096cdf-7202-57cc-a632-c055625d37b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263249} {:answer/id #uuid "7da1c9d4-e363-5fed-ba08-cd3350bed811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264083} {:answer/id #uuid "e47515dc-5670-5487-907c-2b04a5fa6d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264988} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e39e79-758a-5180-b1de-9ef5ce975ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e47515dc-5670-5487-907c-2b04a5fa6d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264988} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20c3493-b518-5f90-8021-6c1e33bc6aff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7993ea70-2f40-5504-828e-aeb8566a66bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130847" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f389b7a-bb36-5074-8c96-fb1ecf9fa6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263288} {:answer/id #uuid "8241a5d7-02a1-547d-baef-267aa901fd37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264119} {:answer/id #uuid "84a7fac4-e47e-5983-a206-08e59164fb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264139} {:answer/id #uuid "b1263628-59c7-546e-a4af-aac116f01421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} {:answer/id #uuid "c5653eec-b4a3-5077-bd82-07173a4abb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1263628-59c7-546e-a4af-aac116f01421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd48ee5b-7dbe-500d-a87b-ee2f033ad6d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "837dfba2-f78f-5c76-b27f-bb2d2c133624" :question/math-academy-id "q-130860" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200326c6-4e9b-5f9d-8ea8-3c7fd8caa616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263292} {:answer/id #uuid "783d2411-8439-515d-972b-2e98645d0bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264043} {:answer/id #uuid "94702e89-66e6-5edd-9c50-630d134703e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264271} {:answer/id #uuid "96a95a1d-d7ee-55e3-9d5d-b9c01aab924a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264289} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a3316a-6a18-572b-8fbd-42d9ba63f793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94702e89-66e6-5edd-9c50-630d134703e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264271} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f26578-678b-584b-94d3-3bf45adddf76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5d6a7d0-f153-5a48-8ab8-2274611f50fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130862" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef54140-2672-5265-b691-9d3fb2cd1f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327064} {:answer/id #uuid "2e06b7d4-773b-593e-9815-139447a16f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327347} {:answer/id #uuid "471c510b-7774-5214-a739-2e988dc25336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327553} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b73e26-2fde-583d-8e80-fea1bc66c31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328505} {:answer/id #uuid "c3da354f-f4b4-5dbb-a0bf-56621d302948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471c510b-7774-5214-a739-2e988dc25336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327553} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9822533-fbcf-5b20-a3af-01eaee0b139a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd3b5a32-f5f9-54aa-b2af-a91ccc349130" :question/math-academy-id "q-42767" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026c7004-8494-5ac7-b146-bd83da70b93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326961} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc553fa-6372-54a1-80cf-6f418a317470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327342} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0fb20-5f68-5538-924e-54424e3a674e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-4{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327724} {:answer/id #uuid "80510d9c-0bde-550b-9d76-7c48e94ee945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328040} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ea519f-6c58-5a67-b687-351fe81c79a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "026c7004-8494-5ac7-b146-bd83da70b93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326961} :answer-field/id #uuid "a89561ad-ace0-5390-80f1-311ee4c1f3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e243a04a-20ca-53ba-bf29-0d9f8f727a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42813" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}]}
